{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"gorilloid-broke-arcticfox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:217-254` and generated `docs/mcp-reference.md:54` advertise plan-review P1-P9 while production executes P1-P11 (`plan_review/registry.py:118`, `det_floor.py:1`, `workflow_ops.py:13`). Code-review lifecycle comments across review-kernel, prompting, workflow, and review-workflow modules also contradict the shipped four-pass gate.\n\n## Approach\n\nCorrect the existing canonical tool descriptions and source-local ownership comments, then regenerate the current MCP reference with the existing generator. Do not introduce a second executable review-policy registry.\n\n## Scope\n\n- MCP LLM tool descriptions and affected review/code-review source comments\n- `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`, generated MCP reference, and its tests\n\n## Testing\n\nRegenerate the reference, run its generator test, and assert the canonical descriptions name P1-P11 and the current four-pass lifecycle.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Canonical MCP tool descriptions advertise P1-P11 exactly as implemented.\n- [ ] Canonical code-review comments describe the shipped four-pass execution rather than future, legacy, or single-pass states.\n- [ ] `docs/mcp-reference.md` is regenerated from the corrected source descriptions.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_gen_mcp_reference.py` and focused documentation checks pass without adding a new registry.","id":"ecb4-ceda-e276-4efb","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":2,"tags":["janitor","documentation","mcp","rp21"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Correct canonical review and gate descriptions and regenerate MCP reference"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d